Build the Waitlist Email Notifications feature for the Zip Code Checker app at /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/Zip-Code. This is a major competitive differentiator — no competitor has automated waitlist notifications.

## Step 1: Read the full file first
Read `app/routes/app.waitlist.tsx` completely. Understand:
- Current action intents (update status, delete, bulk ops)
- How entries are displayed (flat table or grouped by zip)
- What state variables exist
- The loader data shape (what zip codes + entries are returned)
- The fetcher pattern used

---

## Step 2: Add "notify-zip" action intent

In the action function, add a new intent handler. Place it before the final fallback return:

```typescript
if (intent === "notify-zip") {
  const zipCode = (formData.get("zipCode") as string)?.trim().toUpperCase();
  if (!zipCode) {
    return json({ error: "No ZIP code specified." });
  }

  const entries = await db.waitlistEntry.findMany({
    where: { shop, zipCode, status: "waiting" },
    select: { id: true, email: true },
  });

  if (entries.length === 0) {
    return json({ action: "notify-zip", zipCode, emails: [], count: 0 });
  }

  // Mark all as notified
  await db.waitlistEntry.updateMany({
    where: { shop, zipCode, status: "waiting" },
    data: { status: "notified" },
  });

  const emails = entries.map((e) => e.email);
  return json({ action: "notify-zip", zipCode, emails, count: emails.length });
}
```

---

## Step 3: Add state for the notification modal

Add these state variables in the component:
```typescript
const [notifyModalOpen, setNotifyModalOpen] = useState(false);
const [notifyResult, setNotifyResult] = useState<{
  zipCode: string;
  emails: string[];
  count: number;
} | null>(null);
const [emailsCopied, setEmailsCopied] = useState(false);
```

Add a `useEffect` to detect when the notify action completes:
```typescript
const fetcherData = fetcher.data as any;
useEffect(() => {
  if (fetcherData?.action === "notify-zip") {
    setNotifyResult({
      zipCode: fetcherData.zipCode,
      emails: fetcherData.emails,
      count: fetcherData.count,
    });
    setNotifyModalOpen(true);
  }
}, [fetcherData]);
```

---

## Step 4: Add "Notify Waitlist" button in the UI

Look at the current UI structure. There are two ways entries might be shown:

**Option A: If entries are shown grouped by ZIP code** — add a "Notify" button next to each ZIP group header.

**Option B: If entries are in a flat table** — add a new section ABOVE the table: a simple inline form with a Select dropdown (populated with unique ZIP codes that have "waiting" entries) and a "Notify Customers" button.

Read the file and apply whichever fits the existing structure. The button should:
1. Show the count of "waiting" customers: "Notify 3 Waiting Customers"
2. Be disabled if count is 0 or if currently loading

The button submit:
```typescript
const handleNotifyZip = (zipCode: string) => {
  const fd = new FormData();
  fd.set("intent", "notify-zip");
  fd.set("zipCode", zipCode);
  fetcher.submit(fd, { method: "POST" });
};
```

If going with Option B (select dropdown), here's the UI:
```tsx
<Card>
  <BlockStack gap="400">
    <Text variant="headingMd" as="h2">Notify Waitlist by ZIP Code</Text>
    <Text as="p" tone="subdued">
      Select a ZIP code to notify all waiting customers that delivery is now available.
      Their status will be updated to "Notified".
    </Text>
    <InlineStack gap="300" align="start" blockAlign="end">
      <div style={{ minWidth: 200 }}>
        <Select
          label="ZIP Code"
          options={[
            { label: "Select a ZIP code...", value: "" },
            ...uniqueWaitingZips.map(z => ({
              label: `${z.zipCode} (${z.count} waiting)`,
              value: z.zipCode,
            })),
          ]}
          value={selectedNotifyZip}
          onChange={setSelectedNotifyZip}
        />
      </div>
      <Button
        variant="primary"
        disabled={!selectedNotifyZip || isNotifying}
        loading={isNotifying}
        onClick={() => selectedNotifyZip && handleNotifyZip(selectedNotifyZip)}
      >
        Notify Waiting Customers
      </Button>
    </InlineStack>
  </BlockStack>
</Card>
```

Where `uniqueWaitingZips` is derived from loader data:
```typescript
const uniqueWaitingZips = useMemo(() => {
  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};
  entries
    .filter((e: any) => e.status === "waiting")
    .forEach((e: any) => {
      counts[e.zipCode] = (counts[e.zipCode] || 0) + 1;
    });
  return Object.entries(counts).map(([zipCode, count]) => ({ zipCode, count }));
}, [entries]);
```

And add state: `const [selectedNotifyZip, setSelectedNotifyZip] = useState("");`

Loading state: `const isNotifying = fetcher.state !== "idle" && fetcher.formData?.get("intent") === "notify-zip";`

---

## Step 5: Add the Notification Result Modal

Add this Modal component (before the closing `</Page>`):

```tsx
<Modal
  open={notifyModalOpen}
  onClose={() => {
    setNotifyModalOpen(false);
    setEmailsCopied(false);
    setSelectedNotifyZip("");
  }}
  title={`Waitlist Notifications Sent — ZIP ${notifyResult?.zipCode ?? ""}`}
  primaryAction={{
    content: "Done",
    onAction: () => {
      setNotifyModalOpen(false);
      setEmailsCopied(false);
      setSelectedNotifyZip("");
    },
  }}
>
  <Modal.Section>
    <BlockStack gap="400">
      {notifyResult && notifyResult.count > 0 ? (
        <>
          <Banner tone="success">
            <Text as="p">
              <strong>{notifyResult.count}</strong> customer
              {notifyResult.count !== 1 ? "s" : ""} marked as{" "}
              <strong>Notified</strong> for ZIP{" "}
              <strong>{notifyResult.zipCode}</strong>.
            </Text>
          </Banner>
          <Text as="p" variant="bodyMd">
            Use the emails below to reach out to your customers and let them
            know you now deliver to their area.
          </Text>
          <TextField
            label="Customer emails"
            value={notifyResult.emails.join(", ")}
            onChange={() => {}}
            multiline={4}
            autoComplete="off"
            readOnly
          />
          <InlineStack gap="300">
            <Button
              onClick={() => {
                navigator.clipboard
                  .writeText(notifyResult.emails.join(", "))
                  .then(() => setEmailsCopied(true));
              }}
            >
              {emailsCopied ? "Copied!" : "Copy Emails"}
            </Button>
            <Button
              url={`mailto:${notifyResult.emails.join(",")}?subject=Great news! We now deliver to ZIP ${notifyResult.zipCode}&body=Hi!%0A%0AWe're excited to let you know that we now deliver to your area (ZIP code ${notifyResult.zipCode}).%0A%0AVisit our store to place your order!`}
              external
            >
              Open in Email Client
            </Button>
          </InlineStack>
        </>
      ) : (
        <Banner tone="warning">
          <Text as="p">
            No waiting customers found for ZIP{" "}
            <strong>{notifyResult?.zipCode}</strong>.
          </Text>
        </Banner>
      )}
    </BlockStack>
  </Modal.Section>
</Modal>
```

